{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552015-the-after-effects-of-vulgar-magic-on-the-witness","id":1552015,"title":"The after-effects of vulgar magic on the Witness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-02T16:27:19-07:00","id":1552015,"title":"The after-effects of vulgar magic on the Witness","content":"Ok, so there are whole swaths of printed text and forum text and arguments amongst friends devoted to the morass that is Coincidental/Vulgar without Witness/Vulgar with Witness, but is there ever any discussion about what happens to the Witness? For the life of me I can't remember anything related to this.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf you have the Delerium, in Dreaming you have the Mists. When a non-affiliated mortal happens to see some vulgar-as-fuck crossfire between two mages, does this person just remember anything, or do they just have a tendency to explain it away?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I've been playing Mage for almost 3 decades and I can't remember if this is addressed. Must be my 40- something great old brain...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T16:48:38-07:00","id":1552019,"title":"","content":"IIRC they remember. However traumatizing the experience may be, it's a completely mundane trauma, handled without rules.<br /> <br /> Probably that's intentional, by the way, as it lets the ST tune the game through the reactions of bystanders. Some people may very well try to rationalize, or completely block the experience, but others will simply not understand it. In fact, even if the Magic is Vulgar, it doesn't imply they'll believe it was magic, they may just think it has an explanation they don't know about, like a magic trick.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's completely on the ST to decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T04:10:08-07:00","id":1552030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552015-the-after-effects-of-vulgar-magic-on-the-witness?p=1552019#post1552019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC they remember. However traumatizing the experience may be, it's a completely mundane trauma, handled without rules.<br /> <br /> Probably that's intentional, by the way, as it lets the ST tune the game through the reactions of bystanders. Some people may very well try to rationalize, or completely block the experience, but others will simply not understand it. In fact, even if the Magic is Vulgar, it doesn't imply they'll believe it was magic, they may just think it has an explanation they don't know about, like a magic trick.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's completely on the ST to decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I remember that when we were playing 2nd edition my character showed, intentionally, her brother some magic and other players were afraid that NPC could loose his mind. So I feel like there is some kind of mechanic for that. (No I did not red whole book nor I remembered all the rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28779-asderuki","name":"Asderuki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T07:37:20-07:00","id":1552073,"title":"","content":"The Witness isn't affected. That's one of the differences between <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> and <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>: in the latter, mortals have an Integrity trait and they have to make a breaking point check whenever they witness something supernatural, such as Supernal Magic. On top of that, <b>Awakening</b> mortals have to contend with something kind of like <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>'s Mists: a clouding of their memories that causes them to misremember what they witnessed. <br /> <br /> The <b>Mage Translation Guide</b> it written to facilitate taking systems from <b>Ascension</b> or <b>Awakening</b> and porting it over to the other; and <b>Awakening</b>'s rules for how Magic affects Witnesses is definitely something that can be ported. <br /> <br /> But again, it's something that would need to be ported in; <b>Ascension</b> doesn't actually have it. <br /> <br /> Well, not unless the Magick was worked by a Marauder. Their Paradox Backlashes tend to be directed against others; and while that's usually &quot;other mages,&quot; I could see a Storyteller ruling that Witnesses get hit if there aren't any other mages to serve as &quot;lightning rods.&quot; That's not something that's likely to come up, though, as the only time you're likely to see Marauder Backlashs in game are when one or more of the players' characters are present. Unless you're running an unusual game, those characters probably won't be Marauders or Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T10:42:42-07:00","id":1552147,"title":"","content":"This is a really good point and I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1006_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1006\" data-vbnamecard=\"1006\">widdershawns</a> is on the money to have thought of this. I never even knew that M:tAw had rules for what happens to the mortals when they see magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T11:11:02-07:00","id":1552151,"title":"","content":"Despite the obvious similarities and links between the two, MtAw is a very different game, and has quite distinct internal reasons on why the witness suffers the effects they do.<br /> <br /> Again, it's not an omission. MtAs doesn't have rules for that because nothing is supposed to happen. Think, as an example, how easy would the Technocracy's work be if they could count on people just forgetting any Magic they see.<br /> <br /> Mages are people who mold reality and belief. While it may be a preference for some people, the themes of the game don't really benefit from the witnesses suffering any particular effect from what they see. MtAw <b>is a game about secrets</b>, and normal humans there are naturally inimical to magic because of a <b>shard of a lovecraftian dimension lodged within their souls</b>. It is not about belief, it is not about Consensus (it doesn't existe there), it simply doesn't follow any of the themes of Ascension.<br /> <br /> It is a pretty good game, though, I recommend. It isn't about switching games, it is about playing another good game in addition to the good game you already play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T15:50:32-07:00","id":1552169,"title":"","content":"Great points <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>! I think for my own sake, I've often wondered about the impact of seeing &quot;the impossible&quot; on the Human psyche. Think say, of the Cargo Cults founded by Pacific Islanders in 1945, who were hunter-gatherer level of technology, watching at the time, the most advanced nations in the world fight a war with each other. Another avenue is the psychology of stage magic: <a href=\"https://www.bps.org.uk/psychologist/experiencing-impossible\" target=\"_blank\">Experiencing the impossible | BPS</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T16:22:11-07:00","id":1552170,"title":"","content":"There certainly is an impact, it just isn't modeled through rules.<br /> <br /> Such an impact depends heavily on circumstance: who's the witness, how's her culture as a whole, and her understanding of the world in particular, what exactly she saw, what explanation, if any, was given, by whom?<br /> <br /> Figuring out those things should inform the reaction without real need for a roll saying it's this or that.<br /> <br /> By the way, &quot;Cargo Cults&quot; aren't the result of some madness or whatnot. Nor are they simply the result of hunter-gatherers witnessing the war. Those cultures specifically had religious beliefs where the gods lived beyond the sea and would return some day, so what they witnessed had an explanation in their world view that justified the creation of the cults. Cults that persist to this day, as is common for religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T11:28:44-07:00","id":1552269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552015-the-after-effects-of-vulgar-magic-on-the-witness?p=1552170#post1552170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There certainly is an impact, it just isn't modeled through rules.<br /> <br /> Such an impact depends heavily on circumstance: who's the witness, how's her culture as a whole, and her understanding of the world in particular, what exactly she saw, what explanation, if any, was given, by whom?<br /> <br /> Figuring out those things should inform the reaction without real need for a roll saying it's this or that.<br /> <br /> By the way, &quot;Cargo Cults&quot; aren't the result of some madness or whatnot. Nor are they simply the result of hunter-gatherers witnessing the war. Those cultures specifically had religious beliefs where the gods lived beyond the sea and would return some day, so what they witnessed had an explanation in their world view that justified the creation of the cults. Cults that persist to this day, as is common for religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense to me. I just figure seeing &quot;The Impossible&quot; should break people's minds more is often shown in Fiction, either via book or media. RPGs in oWoD and NWOD in certain splats are strangely are often better about this than most and have various mechanics, which to me make a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've written a whole novel about a teenage boy losing his mind after watching his friend being resurrected after being shot in the head and suffering from some flavor of PTSD with recurring nightmares... Ultimately leading to his Awakening at the end of the novel. Basically my premise was &quot;What if someone REALLY saw the impossible?&quot; I think hypothetical people who witness battles between mages, without a mind wipe (Obliviate from Harry Potter) would suffer from severe mental issues as a result afterwards. That said, the flavor of game people want and the stories they want to tell really matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T07:15:23-07:00","id":1552280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552015-the-after-effects-of-vulgar-magic-on-the-witness?p=1552269#post1552269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just figure seeing &quot;The Impossible&quot; should break people's minds more is often shown in Fiction, either via book or media.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a genre thing, and that's the key here.<br /> <br /> Many horror stories follow this in some form, since the Gothic, particularly with Poe, but even more since the Cosmic Horror sub-genre from Lovecraft onwards.<br /> <br /> But this isn't based on real life reactions (and people <b>do</b> see the impossible in real life, in many ways, even if what they see isn't as unreal as they think), it is a literary device with a function on the story, and doesn't occur in every story. It depends a lot on the themes of the story. Even many horror stories, maybe most, don't follow it, although it may be hard to notice when the characters are terrorized by a monster anyway.<br /> <br /> What happens is that Mage isn't horror, even if it has horror elements and can be driven in that direction. One of its main themes is the fight to shape the beliefs of people, to make people believe in magic (at least in <b>your</b> magic). This theme, specifically, don't mesh well with the trope of madness and trauma due to witnessing magic.<br /> <br /> Now, this isn't necessarily the best theme for every chronicle. Even in a given chronicle things can change depending on the moment of the game, the context, the mood of the current story. Whenever you feel that witnesses being traumatized will make for a better story, go for it. Just be aware that for some stories it may not be the best decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T20:26:23-07:00","id":1552438,"title":"","content":"To go along with what others have said, Mage: The Ascension has different goals than, say, Mage: The Awakening or Call of Cthulhu. Where the veil of secrecy about the supernatural is as much guarded by psychological barriers in the minds of mundane people.<br /> <br /> MtAs is a game about fighting for the acceptance of Magick as a tangible force in Reality. For that to happen, it must be possible to convince the masses. Whether that's by spreading your belief system...or via demonstration.<br /> <br /> The cost to doing so are eminently practical. First, Paradox cold-cocking the Mage in the side of the head for their hubris. (Up to and including <i>erasing the Mage from existence</i>; poor Tsar Vargo...). Second, because there's an active and wide-ranging techno-Magickal conspiracy that's on the lookout for &quot;Reality Deviance&quot;. Third, because some people react badly to seeing Magick, but in a &quot;mundane&quot; way, up to and including ostracization or hostility (those bands of witch-hunters have to come from <i>somewhere</i>).<br /> <br /> Traditionalists <i>choose</i> to pull their punches and avoid witnesses, because it causes problems. They choose NOT to, when they think overt Magick, or people seeing it, is worth the risk. Especially if it means proving that their Paradigm is true to the skeptical. You don't win the Ascension War without occasionally putting your Arete where your mouth is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T21:13:20-07:00","id":1552625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552015-the-after-effects-of-vulgar-magic-on-the-witness?p=1552438#post1552438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To go along with what others have said, Mage: The Ascension has different goals than, say, Mage: The Awakening or Call of Cthulhu. Where the veil of secrecy about the supernatural is as much guarded by psychological barriers in the minds of mundane people.<br /> <br /> MtAs is a game about fighting for the acceptance of Magick as a tangible force in Reality. For that to happen, it must be possible to convince the masses. Whether that's by spreading your belief system...or via demonstration.<br /> <br /> The cost to doing so are eminently practical. First, Paradox cold-cocking the Mage in the side of the head for their hubris. (Up to and including <i>erasing the Mage from existence</i>; poor Tsar Vargo...). Second, because there's an active and wide-ranging techno-Magickal conspiracy that's on the lookout for &quot;Reality Deviance&quot;. Third, because some people react badly to seeing Magick, but in a &quot;mundane&quot; way, up to and including ostracization or hostility (those bands of witch-hunters have to come from <i>somewhere</i>).<br /> <br /> Traditionalists <i>choose</i> to pull their punches and avoid witnesses, because it causes problems. They choose NOT to, when they think overt Magick, or people seeing it, is worth the risk. Especially if it means proving that their Paradigm is true to the skeptical. You don't win the Ascension War without occasionally putting your Arete where your mouth is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as a quick clarification, Vargo's Paradox backlash was not unequivocally stated to be or presented as his annihilation (which could not be accounted for under all paradigms), just the disappearance of him and his fleet. I understand that you probably used that term colloquially, but semantics matter, especially when it comes to a game like Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T20:25:02-07:00","id":1552666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552015-the-after-effects-of-vulgar-magic-on-the-witness?p=1552019#post1552019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC they remember. However traumatizing the experience may be, it's a completely mundane trauma, handled without rules.<br /> <br /> Probably that's intentional, by the way, as it lets the ST tune the game through the reactions of bystanders. Some people may very well try to rationalize, or completely block the experience, but others will simply not understand it. In fact, even if the Magic is Vulgar, it doesn't imply they'll believe it was magic, they may just think it has an explanation they don't know about, like a magic trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that sort of the line between coincidental and vulgar though? What you can and can't rationalize? Like, a mage could use tarot cards to predict the future, and a Sleeper could rationalize that as just drawing from a deck of cards. From the same sphere, if a mage stopped time in a market square, that would be vulgar, because no Sleeper can possibly rationalize it.<br /> <br /> That's also why some types of normally vulgar magick can become Coincidental on certain occasions (examples given in the book are a healing miracle in a normal place vs a healing miracle in the middle of Mass, or mediumship in a normal place vs mediumship in New Orleans), because the Sleepers in that area haven't adopted the Technocratic paradigm and can rationalize things in a different way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T21:13:11-07:00","id":1552669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552015-the-after-effects-of-vulgar-magic-on-the-witness?p=1552666#post1552666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that sort of the line between coincidental and vulgar though? What you can and can't rationalize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, and <u><b>for this question</b></u>, mostly no.<br /> <br /> The question here is about the effect of witnessing on the witness. Vulgar vs Coincidental isn't about this, it's about how much Paradox the spell produces. Paradox will punish the Mage, it won't do anything (usually) to the witness. If you shoots are ball of chilling darkness from your fingertips in front of witnesses, you'll likely accrue a lot of Paradox, but nothing will stop the witnesses from seeing and remembering the whole shenanigan.<br /> <br /> What defines Paradox, though, isn't rationalization, but <b><i>the fact</i></b> of whatever the witness saw. It comes from people seeing something blatantly impossible, and that thing being Awakened Magic. We can spend pages upon pages of discussion about the metaphysics of Paradox, but at the end of the day the point is that the person saw Sphere Magic that didn't seemed to be something else.<br /> <br /> But that has nothing to do with what the person thinks about what they saw. They may conclude what they saw is probably some special effect, even if it's not. Just as they may think they saw something supernatural, even if it is mundane. They may think about it later and change their minds, reach new conclusions. They may never quite know what they saw and don't even pay it much attention. And they may simply know what they saw, and that what they saw wasn't normal. By the way, they may witness Coincidental Magic and still, for whatever reason, conclude it was impossible (for good or stupid reasons), that won't change if it was Vulgar or Coincidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}